WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.729
Ladybird is now

00:00:01.541 --> 00:00:02.272
in alpha

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.698
Ladybird

00:00:03.745 --> 00:00:05.207
the independent open-source

00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:06.021
web browser built

00:00:05.832 --> 00:00:06.752
from scratch

00:00:06.976 --> 00:00:07.872
has reached its

00:00:07.684 --> 00:00:09.193
first alpha release

00:00:09.718 --> 00:00:10.861
When you pwn

00:00:10.673 --> 00:00:11.144
us

00:00:11.251 --> 00:00:12.052
please tell us

00:00:11.864 --> 00:00:12.642
how so we

00:00:12.454 --> 00:00:13.774
can harden Ladybird

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.646
Ladybird improves quickly

00:00:15.706 --> 00:00:16.601
and until now

00:00:16.413 --> 00:00:17.014
you had to

00:00:16.826 --> 00:00:17.592
build it from

00:00:17.404 --> 00:00:18.276
source to see

00:00:18.088 --> 00:00:18.594
that

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.014
The alpha is

00:00:19.826 --> 00:00:20.945
a rolling channel

00:00:21.005 --> 00:00:21.618
and we’ll be

00:00:21.429 --> 00:00:22.773
pushing out automatic

00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:23.799
updates regularly

00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:24.657
There’s still a

00:00:24.469 --> 00:00:25.247
mountain of work

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:25.884
ahead of us

00:00:25.931 --> 00:00:27.004
but I’m very

00:00:26.816 --> 00:00:27.582
happy that you

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:28.466
can finally try

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:29.693
Ladybird for yourself

00:00:30.222 --> 00:00:31.236
Full story on

00:00:31.047 --> 00:00:31.943
the dashboard
